<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">An Lushan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-lu">Lushan</a> was a general of Sogdian and Turkic descent who commanded powerful frontier armies in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>. Favoured at the court of Emperor Xuanzong, he accumulated control of several military commands. In 755 he launched a rebellion and proclaimed his own dynasty, and he was killed by his own son in 757.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/an-lushan.jpg" alt="An Lushan" width="316" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 书格 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B8%9D%E9%89%B4%E5%9B%BE%E8%AF%B4.Recueil_Historique_des_Principaux_Traits_de_la_Vie_des_Empereurs_Chinois.95%E5%B8%A7%E5%9B%BE.%E5%BD%A9%E7%BB%98%E5%86%8C%E9%A1%B5.%E7%BA%A618%E4%B8%96%E7%BA%AA_(page_19_%E5%AE%A0%E5%B9%B8%E7%95%AA%E5%B0%86)_(%E5%AE%89%E7%A6%84%E5%B1%B1)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
